## Out of Scope

The following are not in scope for this security policy:

- Vulnerabilities in Apple's own frameworks (Foundation Models, HealthKit, NearbyInteraction, CryptoKit) — report those to Apple via [reportanissue.apple.com](https://reportanissue.apple.com)
- Attacks that require physical access to an unlocked, jailbroken device
- Social engineering attacks against users outside the app
- Theoretical vulnerabilities without a plausible attack path
- Issues already publicly known and tracked in open issues

---

## Disclosure Policy

We follow **coordinated disclosure**. Once a fix is ready:

1. We release the fix
2. We publish a security advisory crediting the reporter
3. We add a note in the release changelog

For Tier 1 issues we aim for a fix within **14 days** of confirmation. For Tier 2, **30 days**. We'll communicate honestly if those timelines aren't achievable.

We do not pursue legal action against researchers acting in good faith under this policy.

---

## A Note on Sensitivity

The data this app handles — menstrual cycles, emotional patterns, intimate journal entries — is the kind of data that can cause real harm to real people if exposed. In some jurisdictions, period tracking data has legal implications. We take that seriously. If you find something, please tell us privately. We will take it seriously too.

